From: rpm-build <rpm-build>
Subject: [PATCH] pkgconfig: add -L${libdir}/aws-lc to aws-lc.pc

The aws-lc-sys Rust crate (>= 0.45) auto-detects a system AWS-LC via
pkg-config, but it discards the -l names from the .pc file and probes
the -L directory for "libcrypto.so" before "libcrypto-awslc.so". With
no -L in aws-lc.pc it probes /usr/lib64, where openssl-devel's
libcrypto.so shadows AWS-LC and the crate silently links OpenSSL 3
against AWS-LC headers and bindings.

Point the crate at %{_libdir}/aws-lc, which holds only AWS-LC symlinks
(libcrypto.so -> libcrypto-awslc.so), so it always resolves AWS-LC.
The suffixed -lssl-awslc/-lcrypto-awslc names are kept, so C consumers
see the same flags as before plus one -L that is a no-op for them.
---
  pkgconfig/product.pc.in        | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pkgconfig/product.pc.in b/pkgconfig/product.pc.in
index 3c67704..0405e01 100644
--- a/pkgconfig/product.pc.in
+++ b/pkgconfig/product.pc.in
@@ -7,4 +7,7 @@ Description: AWS-LC (@SOFTWARE_VERSION@)
 URL: https://github.com/aws/aws-lc
 Version: @REPORTED_PKGCONFIG_VERSION@
 Requires: @PRODUCT_PC_REQUIRES@
+# Search path for aws-lc-sys (Rust) system-library auto-detection; the
+# directory holds only AWS-LC symlinks so it cannot resolve to OpenSSL.
+Libs: -L${libdir}/aws-lc
 
